# 10. SOURCE INTEGRATION AND PROVIDER ENGINEERING

Build a proper provider adapter architecture.

Do not write 30 unrelated API request functions directly inside the main API file.

Use a standard provider interface.

Each provider adapter should support the relevant subset of:

- `search_artists`
- `get_artist_identity`
- `get_artist_profile`
- `get_artist_metrics`
- `get_releases`
- `get_public_content`
- `get_events`
- `get_evidence`
- `health_check`

Each adapter must declare:

- Provider ID.
- Provider name.
- Provider category.
- Capabilities.
- Authentication type.
- Configuration schema.
- Required credentials.
- Access restrictions.
- Quota rules.
- Rate limits.
- Retry behaviour.
- Data fields returned.
- Data retention requirements.
- Official documentation URL.
- Implementation status.

Use typed, normalised output models.

## 10.1 Important provider restrictions

Do not treat all public-looking platforms as unrestricted data feeds.

Implement an access policy for every source.

### MusicBrainz

Use its API responsibly.

- Set a descriptive User-Agent.
- Respect the one-request-per-second client limit.
- Cache appropriate metadata.
- Implement retry handling for HTTP 503 responses.
- Do not burst concurrent requests against it.

Documentation:
https://musicbrainz.org/doc/MusicBrainz_API

### YouTube Data API

Build a real quota manager.

Google currently documents a separate default bucket of 100 `search.list` calls per day, with the search query quota resetting at midnight Pacific Time. Pagination also consumes calls.

Implementation requirements:

- Persistent quota counters.
- Pacific Time reset handling.
- Configurable budgets below the provider's assigned allowance.
- Request-cost tracking.
- Search caching.
- Quota-aware seed rotation.
- No calls after budget exhaustion.
- Display quota status in Settings.

Official references:

https://developers.google.com/youtube/data/determine_quota_cost

https://developers.google.com/youtube/v3/guides/quota_and_compliance_audits

### Spotify

Spotify's Development Mode is subject to material access restrictions.

Do not use a Development Mode integration as the basis of a commercial A&R product.

The current published restrictions include Premium requirements, a five-authorised-user limit and a reduced supported endpoint surface for Development Mode integrations.

Implement a gated adapter:

- Clearly distinguish Development Mode and approved commercial access.
- Show current access mode.
- Do not enable a commercially restricted workflow by default.
- Do not bypass the platform's terms.
- Only use the endpoint surface available to the configured access tier.

Official references:

https://developer.spotify.com/blog/2026-02-06-update-on-developer-access-and-platform-security

https://developer.spotify.com/documentation/web-api/concepts/quota-modes

### TikTok

TikTok Research Tools are intended for qualified independent, non-commercial research under eligibility and approval requirements.

Do not assume that a normal TikTok developer account authorises commercial artist discovery.

Do not scrape restricted TikTok data.

Keep Research Tools marked as research-only unless a separate valid commercial product and applicable permission are established.

Official reference:

https://developers.tiktok.com/products/research-api/

### Reddit

Commercial use of Reddit developer tools and data requires permission and an applicable agreement.

Do not run Reddit enrichment as a commercial source unless the required permission has been obtained.

Display the provider's restricted status accurately.

Official reference:

https://support.reddithelp.com/hc/en-us/articles/14945211791892-Developer-Platform-Accessing-Reddit-Data

### Other providers

For Apple Music, Meta platforms, Instagram, Facebook, Deezer, Last.fm, SoundCloud, Discogs, Twitch, Bluesky, Mastodon, Wikipedia, iTunes Search, GDELT, Flickr, Openverse and other catalogue sources:

- Verify the current official API documentation.
- Confirm allowed endpoints.
- Confirm commercial-use rights.
- Confirm authentication requirements.
- Confirm rate limits.
- Confirm permitted data storage and display.
- Respect provider attribution and licensing requirements.

Never use browser scraping or hidden/private endpoints to evade a provider restriction.

## 10.2 Provider fallback behaviour

When a provider is unavailable:

- Record the failure.
- Preserve existing records.
- Continue with other eligible sources.
- Retry according to policy.
- Mark the source as degraded or unavailable.
- Tell the operator what happened.

A single provider outage must not break the entire discovery process.

