# 12. ARTIST IDENTITY RESOLUTION

Identity resolution is central to the product.

An artist may appear with:

- Slightly different names.
- Alternative spellings.
- Different social handles.
- Different release names.
- Multiple platform IDs.
- Incomplete metadata.

Build a matching engine that compares:

- Provider external identifiers.
- Verified official profile links.
- Name similarity.
- Country and location where available.
- Genre compatibility.
- Release metadata.
- Associated artist information.

Use deterministic identifiers first.

Use fuzzy matching only as a supporting signal.

A match should carry a confidence value and explanation.

Do not automatically merge two artists solely because their display names match.

Low-confidence matches should enter a review queue.

Provide an operator action to link or separate identities.

Store the identity-matching history.

